    {
      "heading": "Coefficients and several letters",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Numbers first, as normal. Then each letter, one at a time.",
          "write": "numbers, then letters"
        },
        {
          "say": "2 a cubed b, times 4 a squared b to the 5.",
          "write": "2a³b × 4a²b⁵"
        },
        {
          "say": "2 times 4 is 8. a cubed times a squared is a to the 5.",
          "write": "8,  a⁵"
        },
        {
          "say": "b is b to the 1. So b times b to the 5 is b to the 6.",
          "write": "= 8a⁵b⁶"
        },
        {
          "say": "Dividing works the same. 12 divided by 4 is 3. m to the 7 over m squared is m to the 5.",
          "write": "12m⁷n³ ÷ 4m²n = 3m⁵n²"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Different bases don't combine",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "The laws only work when the bases are the same.",
          "write": "same base only"
        },
        {
          "say": "x cubed times y squared just stays as x cubed y squared.",
          "write": "x³ × y² = x³y²"
        },
        {
          "say": "2 cubed times 3 squared can't be one power. Just work it out: 72.",
          "write": "2³ × 3² = 8 × 9 = 72"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Don't multiply the indices. x cubed times x to the 4 is not x to the 12.",
          "write": "✗ x¹²   ✓ x⁷"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't multiply the bases. 2 cubed times 2 to the 4 is not 4 to the 7.",
          "write": "✗ 4⁷   ✓ 2⁷"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't add the coefficients. 3 times 5 is 15, not 8.",
          "write": "3x⁴ × 5x² = 15x⁶"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't forget the hidden 1. n cubed divided by n is n squared.",
          "write": "n³ ÷ n = n²"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't divide the indices. a to the 8 over a squared is a to the 6.",
          "write": "✗ a⁴   ✓ a⁶"
        }
      ]
    },
